    "stem": "Rekha must walk from house $H$ to a straight path $L$, then to shop $S$. She wants the shortest broken path $H$-$P$-$S$ with $P$ on $L$.\n\nWhich claims correctly describe how to choose $P$? One or more options may be correct.",
    "item_type": "mcq",
    "options": {
      "A": "The answer is the path $L$ itself, so every point on $L$ gives the same shortest length.",
      "B": "Reflect $S$ across $L$ to $S'$, then choose $P$ where segment $HS'$ meets $L$.",
      "C": "That point $P$ makes $H$-$P$-$S$ equal in length to the straight segment $HS'$.",
      "D": "Choose $P$ as the foot of the perpendicular from the midpoint of $HS$ onto $L$."
    },
